
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

## Native pairing-state tests

Run the pure C++ pairing-state tests with PlatformIO Core 6.1.19:

```powershell
$pioExe = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE '.platformio\penv\Scripts\pio.exe'
& $pioExe test -e native -f test_pairing_state
```

On Windows, use a C++17-capable MinGW compiler. The older optional
`toolchain-gccmingw32` package provides GCC 5.1 and lacks `std::optional`.
The portable compiler used for validation is the x64 UCRT GCC 16.2.0 release
from [WinLibs](https://github.com/brechtsanders/winlibs_mingw/releases/tag/16.2.0posix-14.0.0-ucrt-r2),
with archive SHA-256 `53fb6773fbdf87cdf22b69a6b2a07ee33d3ada413b42d83044bc7cc6481400d2`.
After extracting it under `.pio/native-tools/winlibs-16.2.0-ucrt-r2`, run the
command in PowerShell with its compiler directory temporarily first on `PATH`:

```powershell
$pairingTestOldPath = $env:PATH
$pairingTestOldEncoding = $env:PYTHONIOENCODING
try {
    $nativeCompilerBin = (Resolve-Path .pio/native-tools/winlibs-16.2.0-ucrt-r2/mingw64/bin).Path
    $pioExe = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE '.platformio\penv\Scripts\pio.exe'
    $env:PATH = $nativeCompilerBin + ';' + $pairingTestOldPath
    $env:PYTHONIOENCODING = 'utf-8'
    & $pioExe test -e native -f test_pairing_state
} finally {
    $env:PATH = $pairingTestOldPath
    if ($null -eq $pairingTestOldEncoding) {
        Remove-Item Env:PYTHONIOENCODING -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    } else {
        $env:PYTHONIOENCODING = $pairingTestOldEncoding
    }
}
```

## Direct web-validation tests

The standalone web-validation test currently runs 60 checks. With the WinLibs
toolchain extracted under `.pio/native-tools/winlibs-16.2.0-ucrt-r2`, compile
and run it directly from the repository root:

```powershell
$webValidationOldPath = $env:PATH
try {
    $nativeCompilerBin = (Resolve-Path .pio/native-tools/winlibs-16.2.0-ucrt-r2/mingw64/bin).Path
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path .pio/test-results -Force | Out-Null
    $webValidationTest = Join-Path (Resolve-Path .pio/test-results).Path 'web-validation-tests.exe'
    $env:PATH = $nativeCompilerBin + ';' + $webValidationOldPath
    & (Join-Path $nativeCompilerBin 'g++.exe') -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc `
        .\test\test_web_validation\test_main.cpp .\src\webValidation.cpp -o $webValidationTest
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Web-validation test compilation failed.' }
    & $webValidationTest
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Web-validation tests failed.' }
} finally {
    $env:PATH = $webValidationOldPath
}
```

The executable prints the individual results and a pass/fail total. It checks
pure validation helpers; it does not exercise the running HTTP server or prove
all HTTP security behavior.

The source-owned extended-advertising transition contract also has a read-only
static regression. It verifies that explicit C3 stop completion uses the
successful NimBLE stop return plus inactive state, while spontaneous
ADV_COMPLETE callbacks remain distinct. Run it from PowerShell 7 before a C3 build:

```powershell
pwsh -NoProfile -File .\test\verify-advertising-stop-completion.ps1
```

## Browser control regression checks

Run the inline browser script against the focused Node DOM stub:

```powershell
node .\test\web_ui_regression.cjs
```

This checks polling synchronization, preserved edits, worker feedback, pairing
controls and error recovery. It does not replace the Edge/device acceptance
checklist or test browser layout.
